{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs","id":1521590,"title":"Easy carnivore option for PU 6~7 wuffs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-29T07:47:47-07:00","id":1521590,"title":"Easy carnivore option for PU 6~7 wuffs","content":"Fish.<br /> <br /> No, I'm not kidding. A lot of fish are actually carnivores, and not just sharks or piranha. Bass, cod, swordfish, tuna... yeah, those and more on the menu for Uratha that require carnivore meat, and as expensive as tuna gets, it's probably less of a headache to get than things like, I dunno cat or gator or snake meat or whatever. Other marine animals likely count as well, possibly including a good number of shellfish.<br /> <br /> Probably still requires that the meat be raw... but that just means sashimi and poke bowls are still on the menu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27777-danielxcutter","name":"danielxcutter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T07:57:18-07:00","id":1521591,"title":"","content":"If you're having high primal urge Uratha drive down to the super market and purchase Tuna you and I have very different views of this game. But that's okay, there's room for multiple view points in roleplaying games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T09:53:02-07:00","id":1521598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521591#post1521591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're having high primal urge Uratha drive down to the super market and purchase Tuna you and I have very different views of this game. But that's okay, there's room for multiple view points in roleplaying games.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but using a boat to going fishing your meal in the middle of the sea is surely more in tune with &quot;The wolf must hunt&quot; and still more easy and socially accettable than going in the woods hunting foxes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T10:07:38-07:00","id":1521600,"title":"","content":"Now to decide if they're just sitting with their rod in the water, dynamite fishing, or diving in with a knife between their teeth to duel the sea for their dinner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T11:13:23-07:00","id":1521604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521598#post1521598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but using a boat to going fishing your meal in the middle of the sea is surely more in tune with &quot;The wolf must hunt&quot; and still more easy and socially accettable than going in the woods hunting foxes</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got to drive hundreds of miles to go to anywhere I'd have a chance to fish for tuna where as I've got woods deep enough to hunt in that I drive by every day going back and forth to work. Likewise, we're talking about werewolves, not were-seals, I don't think &quot;the wolf must hunt&quot; really intended &quot;the wolf must hunt in human form using a fishing rod.&quot; <br /> <br /> I also doubt the Uratha are terribly concerned with &quot;socially acceptable.&quot; They gain power by committing acts of cannibalism after all.<br /> <br /> And as to the dynamite... I'm pretty sure the predator kings would like to have a word with you about profaning the sacred hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T11:29:03-07:00","id":1521605,"title":"","content":"Notably, the feeding restriction that comes with Primal Urge has no mandate that food must be obtained by means of hunt, just simply that certain forms of food (meat) are the only things that provide nourishment-so a werewolf could go empty out their local grocery store all they want and be fine as that actual mandate goes. And as for hunt, any definition of it that permits anything as simple as a knife basically has no reason to not count a fishing rod, though admittedly any actual Siskur-Dah is <i>probably </i>not going to see it's utilization (kudos if you find a way to thread the needle of having to without the players just taking the dive).<br /> <br /> As for the Predator Kings, 1) Nothing about their Sacred Prey precludes technology like dynamite being involved with the hunt, and as has been pointed out in Shunned By the Moon and by the writers, the Tribal Ban has some room to negotiate what it means-they might be more upset that the dynamite was not made by the werewolf in question, and 2) meanwhile the Iron Masters are going &quot;Ha ha, fish in the creek go boom.&quot;*<br /> <br /> *Except ecological consequences for that that the Masters are likely to be aware of and act in regard to, particularly if the fishing spot in question is their territory, but that's not funny, so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T12:02:17-07:00","id":1521608,"title":"","content":"So, weird question but seems appropriate:<br /> <br /> Do folks think catfish noodling would be more of a Blood Talon thing (as a demonstration of their physical prowess), or a Storm Lord thing (their whole deal with undergoing harsh trials and ordeals to test their worth)?<br /> <br /> For those unaware, catfish noodling is a fishing practice that involves letting a catfish try to swallow one of your limbs, and then you pull it out of the water while it's trying to gnaw your limb off. The most common target is the flathead, a large catfish (can easily grow over 100 lbs) that's one of the few carnivores in an otherwise more omnivorous group; it's strong predatory instincts is why it's so easy to bait into trying to eat your arm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T12:29:44-07:00","id":1521610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521605#post1521605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notably, the feeding restriction that comes with Primal Urge has no mandate that food must be obtained by means of hunt, just simply that certain forms of food (meat) are the only things that provide nourishment-so a werewolf could go empty out their local grocery store all they want and be fine as that actual mandate goes. And as for hunt, any definition of it that permits anything as simple as a knife basically has no reason to not count a fishing rod, though admittedly any actual Siskur-Dah is <i>probably </i>not going to see it's utilization (kudos if you find a way to thread the needle of having to without the players just taking the dive).<br /> <br /> As for the Predator Kings, 1) Nothing about their Sacred Prey precludes technology like dynamite being involved with the hunt, and as has been pointed out in Shunned By the Moon and by the writers, the Tribal Ban has some room to negotiate what it means-they might be more upset that the dynamite was not made by the werewolf in question, and 2) meanwhile the Iron Masters are going &quot;Ha ha, fish in the creek go boom.&quot;*<br /> <br /> *Except ecological consequences for that that the Masters are likely to be aware of and act in regard to, particularly if the fishing spot in question is their territory, but that's not funny, so.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but if i remember it rightly eating processed food is a breaking point toward spirit, so i would prefer any form of fishing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T12:33:40-07:00","id":1521611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521604#post1521604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've got to drive hundreds of miles to go to anywhere I'd have a chance to fish for tuna where as I've got woods deep enough to hunt in that I drive by every day going back and forth to work. Likewise, we're talking about werewolves, not were-seals, I don't think &quot;the wolf must hunt&quot; really intended &quot;the wolf must hunt in human form using a fishing rod.&quot;<br /> <br /> I also doubt the Uratha are terribly concerned with &quot;socially acceptable.&quot; They gain power by committing acts of cannibalism after all.<br /> <br /> And as to the dynamite... I'm pretty sure the predator kings would like to have a word with you about profaning the sacred hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, i understand.<br /> In my country instead i m half an hour of drive from sea, but i must drive two hours to find a forest with a large population of carnivores.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T12:40:44-07:00","id":1521613,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't think most of us went into this with the assumption that it would be a viable method for <i>everyone</i>. It's just a neat possibility for sea-wolves (and... catfish noodlers, apparently?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T12:57:47-07:00","id":1521615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521608#post1521608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, weird question but seems appropriate:<br /> <br /> Do folks think catfish noodling would be more of a Blood Talon thing (as a demonstration of their physical prowess), or a Storm Lord thing (their whole deal with undergoing harsh trials and ordeals to test their worth)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Living in an area where this is not uncommon and knowing no small number of people who do it? Both. The Blood Talons are all &quot;look what I can do&quot; and the Storm Lords are all &quot;if you can do it, it can't be that hard, hold my Budweiser.&quot; <br /> <br /> I wonder exactly how strictly the carnivore thing applies and exactly what definition carnivore should use. Does it only apply to obligate carnivores or would uncle Bob who doesn't want any of that rabbit food cause &quot;I'm a carnivore, not a rabbit&quot; suffice... Would a venus fly trap count? A high primal urge vegetarian Uratha farmer that raises venus fly traps, pitcher plants, etc. only to eat them because they're the only carnivorous foods available to him would be a ... unique ... character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T13:07:43-07:00","id":1521616,"title":"","content":"I vote in favor of Uncle Bob, since the effort that would have to go into that kind of dedicated cultivation -and it <i>would</i> be dedicated, as keeping that many insectovore plants cultivated in sufficient quantities to keep a person fed would be a huge undertaking- fulfills the spirit of &quot;high Urge shouldn't be easy to circumvent&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T13:18:07-07:00","id":1521618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521608#post1521608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, weird question but seems appropriate:<br /> <br /> Do folks think catfish noodling would be more of a Blood Talon thing (as a demonstration of their physical prowess), or a Storm Lord thing (their whole deal with undergoing harsh trials and ordeals to test their worth)?<br /> <br /> For those unaware, catfish noodling is a fishing practice that involves letting a catfish try to swallow one of your limbs, and then you pull it out of the water while it's trying to gnaw your limb off. The most common target is the flathead, a large catfish (can easily grow over 100 lbs) that's one of the few carnivores in an otherwise more omnivorous group; it's strong predatory instincts is why it's so easy to bait into trying to eat your arm.</div> </div> </div> </div><img width=\"338\" height=\"208\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.tenor.com/odyVsZbC-OYAAAAC/why-not-both-why-not.gif\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.tenor.com/odyVsZbC-OYAAAAC/why-not-both-why-not.gif\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.tenor.com/odyVsZbC-OYAAAAC/why-not-both-why-not.gif\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> If I had to pick one over the other, probably the Storm Lord, since the physical prowess of the Talons isn't as big a deal to them as the Lord's deal to proving their worth through trials and ordeals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521610#post1521610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but if i remember it rightly eating processed food is a breaking point toward spirit, so i would prefer any form of fishing</div> </div> </div> </div>Processed food is a problem for any werewolf deep on the road to Spirit imbalance (it's listed as a breaking point for werewolves at 3 or less), and is a breaking point towards Flesh, so it's arguably a <i>good</i> <i>thing</i> at that point.<br /> <br /> Still, I wouldn't begrudge a werewolf taking the long way on this anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-29-2023, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T15:27:45-07:00","id":1521623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521615#post1521615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Would a venus fly trap count? A high primal urge vegetarian Uratha farmer that raises venus fly traps, pitcher plants, etc. only to eat them because they're the only carnivorous foods available to him would be a ... unique ... character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never have I thought \u2018vegetarian werewolf\u2019 would be a genuinely creepy image <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T17:03:46-07:00","id":1521627,"title":"","content":"I don't really think plants work since the step to carnivore still requires it to be meat.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;carnivorous plants&quot; is fairly hyperbolic. Like most plants, their primary nutrition comes from photosynthesis. The animals they eat are effectively vitamin supplements that help them thrive in areas where other plants would struggle. Cats are obligate carnivores, but supplement their diets with plants to aid in digestion. Humans can't really live for extended periods off an all meat diet; you'd need a variety of meat sources just to cover essential micronutrients, and the lack of phytochemicals that you can't get from eat herbivores would result in all sorts of diseases like scurvy over time. Carnivore is not a strict term, so there's a lot of leeway to be had, but there is a pretty easy to define line between organisms that supplement a non-carnivorous diet with some animal tissue, and animals that use meat for a major part of their primary dietary needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T18:38:50-07:00","id":1521636,"title":"","content":"I mean... it's Shadow BS, hyperbole seems as valid a reason as any. Granted, my understanding of Werewolf is cursory at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T19:36:07-07:00","id":1521639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521636#post1521636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean... it's Shadow BS, hyperbole seems as valid a reason as any. Granted, my understanding of Werewolf is cursory at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shadow has understandable principles that it works off of-laws of sympathy and representation, the atavistic inclination towards &quot;wild&quot; icons being stronger, the flow of resonance and the way the spirit lords can shape them, so on and so forth. It's not all laid out and is definitely more obtuse, but it's not like Requiem where it seems like the curses in the Vitae can mutate, warp, conglomerate and divide into whatever particular powerset you care for it to have*.<br /> <br /> THe (Watsonian) obtuseness of it all stems from the fact that, unlike with other games, like Awakening where understanding the nuts and bolts of reality and it's particular bits is the point or Lost where occultic traditions still have dues owed to the commonwealth of freeholds, Forsaken both has more immediately pragmatic concerns on the whole, and also has a lot more sense of boundaries when it comes to spiritual facts. THe Uratha are a very here and now sort of people, so that first part is easy enough to grasp. As for the second part, for every faction that has interest in laying out and mapping the exact mechanics of the Shadow, there's often equal and opposite numbers interested in maintaining the privacy and dignity of the Shadow and it's greatest actors-for every Bone Shadow and Iron Master who wants to pry, there's an equal and opposite amount of Hunters in Darkness and Storm Lords preserving the purity of locations and preserving the honor of actors by not paying overt attention to weakness, and the Fire Touched and Predator Kings are both of those things in equal measure as an ideal.<br /> <br /> Anyways, as for the particular strain of discussion, I'm gonna echo Arms' sense of sense about it-it'd be weird to have the bit between &quot;meat&quot; and &quot;Essence, which we are also using to highly encourage you towards cannibalism&quot; to be &quot;weird vegetarian alternative friendly&quot;<br /> <br /> *Which, to be fair, is kind of on theme for Requiem, where in the diversity of curses <i>is </i>so great that loose and weird results is not only the norm, but part of the Kindred's overarching problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T20:29:20-07:00","id":1521642,"title":"","content":"<i>*reads thread*</i><br /> <br /> Okay I did not expect the discussion to get this big, but here we are.<br /> <br /> I do get that it'd be a hassle to get the right kinds of (raw) seafood in-land for plenty of packs, but it's still an option. It probably <i>is</i> a lot easier for coastal or perhaps urban Uratha than finding gator meat or whatever, though. But as Arcane mentions, the Uratha <i>are</i> fairly pragmatic. The food part is pretty low on the priority list in comparison, so unless it violates a tribal or Lodge Ban going for the seafood option isn't likely to be a big issue. Though... given how humans and spirits work at any stage of dietary restriction there's probably a symbolism aspect to this. Still, even <i>having</i> other options doesn't hurt.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;way too much effort to be strictly efficient&quot; does seem to be a not-uncommon mitigation when it comes to metaphysical discounts, but I doubt carnivorous plants would count unless they're Aether-powered cryptid monsters or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27777-danielxcutter","name":"danielxcutter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T20:59:00-07:00","id":1521643,"title":"","content":"Then let's find a way to grow plants that count as meat! Hey, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1176040-five-pounds-of-meat?p=1178782#post1178782\">those gentleman</a> at the radio station seem amenable enough to the idea. It won't hurt to ask...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T21:21:35-07:00","id":1521644,"title":"","content":"A large theme of werewolf is &quot;it only counts if you think it does.&quot; If things applied literally the Blood Talons couldn't exist and the tribal weaknesses would be iron chains. Vegan bacon, sausage, etc is already a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T21:50:47-07:00","id":1521646,"title":"","content":"I still doubt vegan things would work, though, especially given that there <i>are</i> a couple of relatively hard rules when it comes to the Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27777-danielxcutter","name":"danielxcutter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T23:16:54-07:00","id":1521648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danielxcutter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521642#post1521642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>*reads thread*</i><br /> <br /> Okay I did not expect the discussion to get this big, but here we are..</div> </div> </div> </div>If I may offer a defense as far as I am currently interested, my entire interest is that you are actually phenomenally right, and even in a way I would deem really narratively interesting-albeit in a bit of a NPC sense.<br /> <br /> See, the thing is, you've set a premise for a a character who is one of those worst-case-scenarios NPC's to be, in the same vein as the Lady of the Light from Alan Wake. It's functional and really viable, and even outside of my parameters just really usable. Is any of it desirable? THe answer to that is even more broadly variable even if the broad answer is also no, and that conflict is Very Much Why I'm Here.<br /> <br /> See, the thing of the matter is that, for me personally, you've managed to find a negotiable middle ground to &quot;suffienciently powerful enough to resolve own personal problems&quot; with &quot;being at all existentially concerned with anyone else outside of yourself&quot; at a scale I still find personably relatable. Six to seven is about that scale across the board, and the thing of the matter is that this particular case is pretty interpretable-notice no one has mention &quot;nourishable within the confines of what a human needs&quot; against &quot;nourishable assuming metaphysical bullshit&quot; as a metric. Those two boundaries create a lot of creative and interesting playspace that is, within my reason of limited knowledge, really fun to play around with, because it lets you lay out a way of ways to think about the problem actually in play, and then let you narrow down into a particular expression of conflict, which highlights any of the larger problems at play.<br /> <br /> To me, that's very much what I like about the franchise-creative answers to problems that engender new questions of conflicts that require you to first gain an appreciation of the older conflicts in play, and consider what is the best answer that accomodates all answers. Humanity is all about recognizing all elements at play, and a good answer to one problem needs to be seen as a problem in other ways and thus recognized on a wholer thing than beyond humanity.<br /> <br /> Notably, and to counter-argue Shadowcat here, this idea works all the better against imperical and objective truths, because both the audience and the characters are currently straining against objective truths and how much subjectivity can bend us around certain facts. As I mentioned earlier, the Shadow has objective laws, and the relationship between the Flesh, the Gauntlet, and the Shadow has objective consequences-but how much of the case around those has room for Storyteller Fiat, so you can tell this story any number of ways. In the scores of Forsaken one shots I've run over the years (and why is it Forsaken I absolutely know but is fun to &quot;lament&quot; about all the same), I've taken so many myriad points of view on I'm not even sure i can properly list them.<br /> <br /> Let me put it another way. I've seen so many &quot;answers&quot; to any given gameline, I could fucking snore as a given. You've provided basically the premise for a Night Horrors character, and that's inarguably high praise given how I got into the industry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-30-2023, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T04:51:46-07:00","id":1521659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521648#post1521648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Shadlecatz</div> </div> </div> </div>Excuse the fuck out of you? I have not once called you by any name except your chosen nor have I disrespected your chosen pronouns, you can show the same courtesy. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T06:34:35-07:00","id":1521661,"title":"","content":"That... looks like it was just a typo? L is close to O on phone keyboards, as is W and E. What would Shadle even mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T07:11:38-07:00","id":1521662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521661#post1521661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That... looks like it was just a typo? L is close to O on phone keyboards, as is W and E. What would Shadle even mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doubtful, her spelling / typing is fine outside of that, one letter, that could be a typo, 3 in a single name in an otherwise properly spelt and typed post is unlikely . <br /> <br /> As to what it means? I suspect nothing, it was just her being disrespectful because we've disagreed previously and because I ignored her disagreeing with me in this thread earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T07:18:40-07:00","id":1521663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521662#post1521662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doubtful, her spelling / typing is fine outside of that, one letter, that could be a typo, 3 in a single name in an otherwise properly spelt and typed post is unlikely .<br /> <br /> As to what it means? I suspect nothing, it was just her being disrespectful because we've disagreed previously and because I ignored her disagreeing with me in this thread earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>... I disagree with Ark all the time, that doesn't tend to be how she operates. And given that she typed up a block of text, misspelling someone's username really isn't THAT out there.<br /> <br /> Maaaybe take a step back and consider whether the &quot;<a href=\"https://en.m.wiktionary.org/wiki/bitch_eating_crackers#:~:text=bitch%20eating%20crackers%20(plural%20bitches,makes%20one%20angry%20or%20annoyed.\" target=\"_blank\">bitch eating crackers</a>&quot; principle is in effect here, and whether it might be simpler to just put Ark on your block list. While it can feel like running away from a &quot;fight&quot; its worth remembering that this is the internet, none of our opinions on a game really matter at the end of the day, and sincerely yelling into the void is just liable to strain your voice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T08:36:25-07:00","id":1521664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521663#post1521663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... I disagree with Ark all the time, that doesn't tend to be how she operates.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There seems to be clear evidence to the contrary. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And given that she typed up a block of text, misspelling someone's username really isn't THAT out there. </div> </div> </div>Remember, she's a professional, as she pointed out to me in our last interaction, and that includes typing. I doubt she would get very far having 3 spelling errors in 1 word. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maaaybe take a step back and consider whether the &quot;<a href=\"https://en.m.wiktionary.org/wiki/bitch_eating_crackers#:~:text=bitch%20eating%20crackers%20(plural%20bitches,makes%20one%20angry%20or%20annoyed.\" target=\"_blank\">bitch eating crackers</a>&quot; principle is in effect here, and whether it might be simpler to just put Ark on your block list. While it can feel like running away from a &quot;fight&quot; its worth remembering that this is the internet, none of our opinions on a game really matter at the end of the day, and sincerely yelling into the void is just liable to strain your voice. </div> </div> </div>You really think the person who is asking to be treated with the bare minimum of respect is the one in the wrong here? Really? Why don't you look into why you're white knighting for her rather than letting her speak for herself whenever she happens to come back?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T10:10:11-07:00","id":1521674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521659#post1521659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Excuse the fuck out of you? I have not once called you by any name except your chosen nor have I disrespected your chosen pronouns, you can show the same courtesy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies, I was drunk when writing and apparently let old Achievement Hunter videos take over the writing. I have corrected the original post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T10:19:41-07:00","id":1521676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521674#post1521674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Apologies, I was drunk when writing and apparently let old Achievement Hunter videos take over the writing. I have corrected the original post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I apologize for my response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T10:21:52-07:00","id":1521678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521676#post1521676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then I apologize for my response.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a fair reaction with the information available, I can't get mad about it.<br /> <br /> Anyways, back on track, I suppose the next productive thing is to explore other option for the carnivore-confined culinary canine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-30-2023, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T10:55:32-07:00","id":1521682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521664#post1521664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...you're white knighting...</div> </div> </div> </div><img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1298_1693435661558_46\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1298\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1298\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1298&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b<br /> Oh, you <i>are</i> precious, aren't you? Yeah, no, if your first response to pushback is to start going ad hominim, then I'm just gonna save myself some headache and follow my own block-list advice.<br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> Parasitic mushrooms, maybe? Or <a href=\"https://www.livescience.com/magic-mushroom-injection-case-report.html\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-30-2023, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T11:46:02-07:00","id":1521684,"title":"","content":"Now I'm imagining a wolf blooded (or perhaps even an Iron Master) working in a research lab attempting to grow meat in a vat. I wonder would &quot;carnivore&quot; meat count if the meat was never actually part of the carnivore species it comes from? If so, looping back around to the original topic, I think fish meat, perhaps especially tuna, would be the optimal choice, it might receive less funding than beef or chicken would, but you're going to get a lot less questions trying to grow tuna meat in a petri dish than you would trying to grow, say, house cat meat.<br /> <br /> Maybe you could even share a lab with the ghoul working on artificial blood substitutes...<br /> <br /> ETA: Of course, if you could develop a substitute for human flesh and provide the Uratha with virtually unlimited essence..... Aren't there already experiments trying to grow human hearts in animals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T13:39:25-07:00","id":1521691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521684#post1521684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ETA: Of course, if you could develop a substitute for human flesh and provide the Uratha with virtually unlimited essence..... Aren't there already experiments trying to grow human hearts in animals?</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I'm of the mind that I think for supernatural purposes, there <i>is</i> no substitute for human flesh in spiritual terms. You could, for instance, grow the biological components of human flesh in a controlled laboratory setting but for spiritual reasons, I would not count it as 'human flesh' mechanically - if it does not risk an uratha's Harmony or break that particular Tenet of the Oath, it should not provide the benefits of consuming human flesh either. I could see it as something of a false hope though, pursued by Pure and Forsaken alike, and such experiments could lay the foundations for horrific secrets in their efforts to 'get it right'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T14:02:42-07:00","id":1521695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Firebrand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521691#post1521691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, I'm of the mind that I think for supernatural purposes, there <i>is</i> no substitute for human flesh in spiritual terms. You could, for instance, grow the biological components of human flesh in a controlled laboratory setting but for spiritual reasons, I would not count it as 'human flesh' mechanically - if it does not risk an uratha's Harmony or break that particular Tenet of the Oath, it should not provide the benefits of consuming human flesh either. I could see it as something of a false hope though, pursued by Pure and Forsaken alike, and such experiments could lay the foundations for horrific secrets in their efforts to 'get it right'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. You could do everything from bound spirits and bound ghosts to graphic biological stuff as gross as your table wants. It wouldn't even have to be Forsaken or Pure, a scientist (or even just person who worked in the lab) turned Ghost Wolf Tyrant who drives the other scientists to commit breaking points could be a villain and a half. (Ghost Wolf Tyrants might be my favorite villain in any roleplaying game, bar none.) I hadn't ever really considered technological horror working with the Forsaken but it could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T03:26:19-07:00","id":1521737,"title":"","content":"The way I think about uratha gaining Essence from eating humans and wolves is that humans and wolves are simply Resonant for uratha. Uratha are very spirit-like so it makes sense that they can gain Essence in ways that are similar to spirits. Hunting (other) spirits in accordance with their nature is also something spirits can do (without becoming magaths due to their prey being of different choirs), and the different lunar phases are Resonant with the Auspices. And Loci are literal Essence generators.<br /> The difference between uratha and spirits is that uratha are also physical creatures, so they need to physically ingest flesh to gain the Essence.<br /> Resonance being the cause of this interaction also explains why it's both humans (who are uniquely Essence rich among living beings) and wolves that grants Essence, as well as why it's <i>exclusively</i> humans and wolves. Not even eating other uratha gives Essence because, like all spirit-like beings, they don't generate Essence.<br /> <br /> So, with this in mind, I don't think anything other than a human, or parts taken directly from a human (without being transformed in the process, so no cooked meat) even if there are human-like elements, would grant Essence. Not even human organs grown outside a human, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T15:41:54-07:00","id":1521841,"title":"","content":"I kind of feel bad for suggesting this, but...cat and dogs? would they count?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T16:21:34-07:00","id":1521842,"title":"","content":"Technically? I'm pretty sure they count as hunting carnivores.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T18:16:09-07:00","id":1521843,"title":"","content":"Yes both dogs and cats are carnivores.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T18:41:00-07:00","id":1521847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521841#post1521841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of feel bad for suggesting this, but...cat and dogs? would they count?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Wouldn't be a ravenous monster story without the space for neighborhood pets to go missing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T19:35:40-07:00","id":1523521,"title":"","content":"Okay, I forgot to check into this site for like two months so I didn't see this until just now, but<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1521648#post1521648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I may offer a defense as far as I am currently interested, my entire interest is that you are actually phenomenally right, and even in a way I would deem really narratively interesting-albeit in a bit of a NPC sense.<br /> <br /> See, the thing is, you've set a premise for a a character who is one of those worst-case-scenarios NPC's to be, in the same vein as the Lady of the Light from Alan Wake. It's functional and really viable, and even outside of my parameters just really usable. Is any of it desirable? THe answer to that is even more broadly variable even if the broad answer is also no, and that conflict is Very Much Why I'm Here.<br /> <br /> See, the thing of the matter is that, for me personally, you've managed to find a negotiable middle ground to &quot;suffienciently powerful enough to resolve own personal problems&quot; with &quot;being at all existentially concerned with anyone else outside of yourself&quot; at a scale I still find personably relatable. Six to seven is about that scale across the board, and the thing of the matter is that this particular case is pretty interpretable-notice no one has mention &quot;nourishable within the confines of what a human needs&quot; against &quot;nourishable assuming metaphysical bullshit&quot; as a metric. Those two boundaries create a lot of creative and interesting playspace that is, within my reason of limited knowledge, really fun to play around with, because it lets you lay out a way of ways to think about the problem actually in play, and then let you narrow down into a particular expression of conflict, which highlights any of the larger problems at play.<br /> <br /> To me, that's very much what I like about the franchise-creative answers to problems that engender new questions of conflicts that require you to first gain an appreciation of the older conflicts in play, and consider what is the best answer that accomodates all answers. Humanity is all about recognizing all elements at play, and a good answer to one problem needs to be seen as a problem in other ways and thus recognized on a wholer thing than beyond humanity.<br /> <br /> Notably, and to counter-argue Shadowcat here, this idea works all the better against imperical and objective truths, because both the audience and the characters are currently straining against objective truths and how much subjectivity can bend us around certain facts. As I mentioned earlier, the Shadow has objective laws, and the relationship between the Flesh, the Gauntlet, and the Shadow has objective consequences-but how much of the case around those has room for Storyteller Fiat, so you can tell this story any number of ways. In the scores of Forsaken one shots I've run over the years (and why is it Forsaken I absolutely know but is fun to &quot;lament&quot; about all the same), I've taken so many myriad points of view on I'm not even sure i can properly list them.<br /> <br /> Let me put it another way. I've seen so many &quot;answers&quot; to any given gameline, I could fucking snore as a given. <b>You've provided basically the premise for a Night Horrors character, and that's inarguably high praise given how I got into the industry.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> As someone who is in fact attempting to write a Contagion Chronicle Night Horrors (despite this being enough hubris for at least three Silver Ladder Obrimoi), this is high praise indeed. Thank you.<br /> <br /> Also, so you did writing for CofD then? May I ask what you wrote?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27777-danielxcutter","name":"danielxcutter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T21:30:08-07:00","id":1523527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danielxcutter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1521590-easy-carnivore-option-for-pu-6~7-wuffs?p=1523521#post1523521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">